# Built browser-app bundles are deployment artefacts, not source.
#
# Vercel is not wired to GitHub here: a deploy uploads the working tree, so the
# bytes on disk are the bytes served. core.autocrlf is true on this machine, so
# without this rule a fresh checkout rewrites these bundles with CRLF and the
# repo can no longer reproduce the live site byte for byte. That is how the
# AI Act app drifted untracked from 7 October to 13 November 2026 without
# anything noticing.
#
# -text means: store and check out exactly these bytes, never translate.
# Scoped to public/*/app/ on purpose - the hand-authored pages one level up
# (index.html, privacy.html, support.html, terms.html) are source and stay
# under normal handling.
public/**/app/** -text
